# TK pre-sales standards (always apply)

This workspace produces **two formal TK deliverables** from rough customer input:
a **requirements package** (Output 2) and a **solution architecture & workflow
pack** (Output 3). Both are single, self-contained A4 HTML files stamped
"TK Company – Confidential".

**Skills are the standard, not suggestions.** Load them before writing:

- Requirements work: `tk-ba-requirements` (orchestrator) → `tk-ba-analysis`,
  `tk-ba-scope`, `tk-ba-technical-requirements`, `tk-ba-functional-spec`,
  `tk-ba-user-stories`, `tk-ba-commercial-awareness`.
- Architecture work: `tk-solution-architecture` (orchestrator) →
  `tk-process-modelling`, `tk-platform-tools`, `tk-architecture-rules`,
  `tk-diagram-standards`.
- Both: `tk-doc-a4-confidential` for the document shell.

**Deliverables live in `.codeartsdoer/deliverables/<project>/`** with IDs
`TK-BA-<PROJECT>-REQ-<nn>` and `TK-SA-<PROJECT>-ARC-<nn>`. Keep the raw customer
input there as `input.md` for traceability.

**Non-negotiables**

- **Never silently resolve a stakeholder conflict.** Record it as `OI-` with both
  positions, a decision owner and a due date.
- **Never invent numbers or integrations.** Everything traces to the input;
  unverified figures become `AS-` assumptions with an owner. When two figures are
  given, size with the higher one and flag it.
- **Testability.** Every requirement is one "The system shall …" statement with
  an ID, priority, source and measurable acceptance. If a tester can't write a
  pass/fail test from it, it isn't a requirement yet.
- **Architecture rules.** Channels never touch a database; SAP / POS / marketplace
  traffic only via TK-Connect; every non-TK component needs an ADR; money flows are
  idempotent, reconciled and audited; PDPA data is classified, encrypted, masked
  and retention-bound; peak load is sized with headroom.
- **Document format.** "TK Company – Confidential" in the header AND footer of
  every page with a page number; cover, document control and TOC present; opens
  offline as a single file; prints to A4 with nothing clipped; every diagram is
  inline SVG carrying the in‑SVG "TK CONFIDENTIAL" label.
- **Honest reporting.** Never claim a check or verification passed unless it was
  run in this session and seen to pass.

**Who does what.** Authors: `tk-ba`, `tk-sa`. Verifiers (independent, report-only):
`tk-senior-ba`, `tk-senior-sa`. Final document gate: `tk-doc-qa`. The
`tk-presales-delivery` team scene orchestrates them; the Delivery Lead never writes
the documents itself.

**Language.** Write documents in English by default; keep Thai business terms with
a glossary; keep all IDs, code and file names in English.